# Location-first business search

When changing OpenAI / Places / mission planning code:

- NEVER look up a restaurant or business by brand name alone.
- ALWAYS pass `profile.area`, `profile.latitude`, and `profile.longitude` into search.
- Prefer the nearest location within ~20–25 miles; reject hours-away franchise hits (e.g. Prosper when user is in Liberty Hill).
- See root `AGENTS.md` and `backend/src/services/location.js`.

# Pickup orders need items first

- "call X and make a pickup order" with no menu items → ask what to order before dialing.
- Do not use the direct-call shortcut for restaurant pickup/order placement.
- See `needsOrderItemsBeforeCall` in `backend/src/services/openai.js` and `AGENTS.md`.

# Stay on live calls

- If the callee is unclear, ask them to repeat/clarify — do not hang up mid-call.
- See AGENTS.md "Stay on the line" and `buildMissionCallPrompt` in `backend/src/services/vapi.js`.

# Human greeting on outbound calls

- We say Hi first. ~5s silence (Vapi min) → "Can you hear me?" Once they speak, reply immediately (no dead air).
- Do not volunteer "this is {name}" unless asked. Do not put the order/message in `firstMessage`.
- See AGENTS.md "Human greeting protocol".
